                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f083f65-c7a5-307c-baf8-76c564cda65f",
                        "entry_id": "62f2a6de-526d-35a4-bfb1-4c4faa6630cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Développement volumineux parasitaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e16bd1f-201f-4b68-8f3a-8473fe0adb89",
                                "sense_id": "6f083f65-c7a5-307c-baf8-76c564cda65f",
                                "text": "Au lieu de s’unir comme frères au pied du trône contre les excrescences qui n’ont et ne prétendent que contre notre ordre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4ed795d-45a1-489b-b340-fea8185a88c4",
                                "sense_id": "6f083f65-c7a5-307c-baf8-76c564cda65f",
                                "text": "Ce territoire [Metz, Toul et Verdun] pouvait être regardé comme une excrescence de l’Empire germanique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fcc9ccef-5187-4500-8667-d735412efc37",
                        "source_entry_id": "62f2a6de-526d-35a4-bfb1-4c4faa6630cc",
                        "source_sense_id": "6f083f65-c7a5-307c-baf8-76c564cda65f",
                        "target_lang_word": "excrescence",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "excrescence",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0ca4e6a2-42d8-3300-8e5e-0103f4351fca",
                                        "entry_id": "12b7ff4c-e8ee-3d8e-8b4b-6b57873acd0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something, usually abnormal, which grows out of something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6d28396-9763-4eb0-8114-3f0c86449a48",
                                                "sense_id": "0ca4e6a2-42d8-3300-8e5e-0103f4351fca",
                                                "text": "I have again and again intimated that I desire the hair to be arranged closely, modestly, plainly. Miss Temple, that girl’s hair must be cut off entirely; I will send a barber to-morrow: and I see others who have far too much of the excrescence—that tall girl, tell her to turn round."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f987ab48-24a5-4924-a259-65aeb0033959",
                                                "sense_id": "0ca4e6a2-42d8-3300-8e5e-0103f4351fca",
                                                "text": "The squirrels were in hiding. One only he saw,—a sleek gray fellow, flattened against a gray dead limb so that he seemed a part of it, a woody excrescence upon the wood itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f590e7d-2bc7-41cf-a6f5-df5cf5386768",
                                                "sense_id": "0ca4e6a2-42d8-3300-8e5e-0103f4351fca",
                                                "text": "Perhaps he meant that towns are after all excrescences, grey fluxions, where men, hurrying to find one another, have lost themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b610478-eefc-443b-b43f-f9a25efe8d43",
                                                "sense_id": "0ca4e6a2-42d8-3300-8e5e-0103f4351fca",
                                                "text": "It is taken for granted that a beggar does not 'earn' his living, as a bricklayer or a literary critic 'earns' his. He is a mere social excrescence, tolerated because we live in a humane age, but essentially despicable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba6e2e5c-c8d8-37a9-b679-e6fed8b7f5c0",
                                        "entry_id": "12b7ff4c-e8ee-3d8e-8b4b-6b57873acd0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A disfiguring or unwanted mark or adjunct."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64a476d9-4637-4a34-b707-dca3155e49be",
                                                "sense_id": "ba6e2e5c-c8d8-37a9-b679-e6fed8b7f5c0",
                                                "text": "Being bussum buddies, the two friends often communicated with mere exchange of psychic forces, verbal communication having been rendered unnecessary excrescence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e9d9661-db30-3280-9eb4-df04961a359e",
                                        "entry_id": "12b7ff4c-e8ee-3d8e-8b4b-6b57873acd0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The epenthesis of a consonant, e.g., warmth as [ˈwɔrmpθ] (adding a [p] between [m] and [θ]), or -t (Etymology 2)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
